@factions
title: Internal factions
on-arrival: {!
for (const faction of [
    "barons", "spring", "labor", "progressives", "razem", "pps",
    "social_patriot"
]) {
    Q[faction + "_strength"] = Math.max(
        0,
        Math.min(100, Number(Q[faction + "_strength"]) || 0)
    );
    Q[faction + "_dissent"] = Math.max(
        0,
        Math.min(100, Number(Q[faction + "_dissent"]) || 0)
    );
}
!}

= Internal factions

Strength controls a faction's leverage. Dissent controls its willingness to
rebel. Editing an inactive faction does not activate it or rewrite its
story-driven membership.

<div class="ledger-section">
<div class="ledger-row"><b>[+ barons_name +]</b><span>strength [+
barons_strength +] · dissent [+ barons_dissent +][? if not barons_active: ·
inactive?]</span></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><b>[+ spring_name +]</b><span>strength [+
spring_strength +] · dissent [+ spring_dissent +][? if not spring_active: ·
inactive?]</span></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><b>[+ labor_name +]</b><span>strength [+ labor_strength
+] · dissent [+ labor_dissent +][? if not labor_active: · inactive?]</span></div>
